// A user belongs to any number of workspaces and carries a different set of roles in each, so
// every authorization-bearing row hangs off the *membership*, never off the user. That is the
// whole shape of this schema: `WorkspaceMember` is the principal for authorization, `User` is
// the principal for authentication.
//
// Sessions and the access token stay user-level and workspace-agnostic on purpose — a request
// names the workspace it is acting in (X-Workspace-Id), the guard resolves the membership on the
// `[userId, workspaceId]` unique index, and the permissions that membership carries *there* are
// read from the database on that request. The token carries no authorization at all.
//
// Table and column names are snake_case/plural at the database level and camelCase in TypeScript;
// Prisma maps between them, so nothing in the application code spells a column name.
// simple-auth-kit's schema is split by domain across the files in database/schema/ (this one
// holds only the generator and datasource). Prisma's multi-file schema support merges every
// .prisma file under database/schema/ into one logical schema — so a consumer's own models go in
// their own file there under a name the kit doesn't use (e.g. app.prisma), which the CLI never
// touches: it only manages the files it installed, tracked by name in auth.lock.json.
//
// `output` stays relative to *this file's own location*: "../generated/prisma" (one level up
// from database/schema/) lands at database/generated/prisma — true both for the registry's own
// dev/typecheck loop (scripts/materialize.mjs keeps database/ a sibling of src/) and for a real
// CLI install (prisma.config.ts + database/ move to the project root together, as one unit).
// Source imports the generated client via the stable "@/database/*" alias rather than a relative
// path, so nothing needs rewriting on install the way the old top-level generated/ did.
generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client"
  output   = "../generated/prisma"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}
